Package: [[name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is the
# agent module's version with -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~SNAPSHOT, which sorts below the release
# rather than above it.
Version: [[agent.package.version]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: fuin.org <info@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/fuinorg/sokar
Depends: sokar
Description: [[description]] [[agent.cli.version]]
 Installs into /usr/libexec/sokar/agents, where the sokar binary looks for
 agents. Nothing needs to be registered: sokar scans that directory and asks
 whatever it finds to describe itself, so installing this package is enough.
 .
 Oh My Pi is https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi, invoked as "omp". It is not
 the Pi that sokar-agent-pi carries, which is https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
 and is invoked as "pi". The two packages share no file.
 .
 The package version is this agent's own version, independent of Sokar's release
 line. The agent CLI version it installs is on the Description line above, so
 "dpkg -s sokar-agent-omp" answers which Oh My Pi this package fetches, without
 consulting the definition.
